{"type": "FeatureCollection", "metadata": {"note": "The Burlington's line west and northwest from Lincoln through the Nebraska Sand Hills to Alliance, then up through Crawford, Edgemont, Newcastle, Gillette and Sheridan and on into Montana -- the road that took the CB&Q into the eastern Wyoming coalfields and gave it a connection with James J. Hill's northern transcontinentals. Construction northwest from Alliance began November 1888; the rails reached Sheridan November 22 1892. Building north of Sheridan started in June 1893 but stalled when the economy crashed later that year, resuming April 1894 and reaching Montana that August. The CB&Q met the Northern Pacific at Huntley, Montana on October 28 1894, opening the through route into Billings. That connection is a large part of why Hill's Great Northern and the Northern Pacific bought nearly all of the Burlington's stock in 1901. GEOMETRY IS A REAL TRACE from OpenStreetMap (railway=rail, usage=main), routed with non-BNSF track penalised 12x so the path stays on the CB&Q's successor's rails; it runs 100% on BNSF, through the Ravenna, Sand Hills, Butte, Black Hills and Big Horn Subdivisions, which are the ex-CB&Q route. Simplified to a 30 m Douglas-Peucker tolerance. Zero reversal or revisit artifacts. Passes within 2.8 km of Lincoln, Ravenna, Alliance, Edgemont, Newcastle, Gillette, Sheridan, Hardin and Billings. NOTE ON THE BILLINGS END: the CB&Q's own rails ended at Huntley; the last ~14 miles into Billings were over the Northern Pacific, and are drawn here as part of the through route. A short junction wye at Huntley that the router picked up has been trimmed so the line runs straight through the junction.", "sources": ["https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/burlington-route-wyomings-second-transcontinental-railroad and https://www.american-rails.com/cbq.html (CB&Q began building northwest from Alliance, Nebraska in November 1888; reached Sheridan, Wyoming November 22 1892; construction north of Sheridan began June 1893, stalled in the Panic of 1893, resumed April 1894, reaching Montana and the Crow Reservation that August; connected with the Northern Pacific at Huntley, Montana October 28 1894, opening the through route to Billings; the line ran northwest from Alliance through the coalfields of eastern Wyoming)", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago,_Burlington_and_Quincy_Railroad (Hill's Great Northern with the Northern Pacific held nearly 100 percent of Burlington stock by 1901; Burlington Northern merger March 2 1970)", "OpenStreetMap via Overpass (railway=rail, usage=main, bbox 40.60/-109.10 to 46.10/-96.40), retrieved 2026-08-25; base data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL"], "not_yet_sourced": "All frequencies are estimated. The dates given are for the Alliance-Billings construction; the Lincoln-Alliance portion east of Alliance was in place by the late 1880s but its own opening dates are not separately sourced here, so the whole line is shown from 1888. Terminal trackage at both ends is modern.", "pulled": "20260825", "passenger_end_correction": "2026-08-30: the feature previously ran to 1971 with a 1970-1971 segment asserting 'Amtrak took over intercity passenger service in 1971'. Amtrak never ran Lincoln - Alliance - Billings; the last scheduled passenger train over Alliance - Sheridan - Billings was 24 August 1969 (WyoHistory.org). The 1970-1971 segment was removed and the preceding segment now ends 1969. Source: research/branches/chicago_burlington_and_quincy_railroad.txt, EXISTING LAYER CHECK."}, "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad", "line": "Chicago, Burlington and Quincy: Lincoln – Alliance – Billings", "id": "cbq-lincoln-alliance-billings", "color": "#8E1B3C", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 58, "speed_source": "estimated: long plains and mountain-division main line, heavy coal traffic; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1888, "end": 1894, "headway_min": 720, "note": "Construction northwest from Alliance began November 1888, pushing into the eastern Wyoming coalfields and reaching Sheridan November 22 1892; work north of Sheridan began June 1893, stalled in the Panic of 1893 and resumed April 1894; frequency estimated/unsourced"}, {"start": 1894, "end": 1901, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Through route opened in 1894, the CB&Q meeting the Northern Pacific at Huntley, Montana on October 28 1894 for the final run into Billings; frequency estimated/unsourced"}, {"start": 1901, "end": 1969, "headway_min": 360, "note": "From 1901 the Burlington was controlled by Hill's Great Northern and the Northern Pacific, who together held nearly all its stock -- this line being the physical connection that made the Burlington worth buying. NOTE the 1901 stock purchase did NOT change who ran the trains: the CB&Q kept its own name, crews and timetable until the 1970 Burlington Northern merger, so this is not an operator change under Rule 4. THE LAST SCHEDULED PASSENGER TRAIN from Alliance, Neb., through Sheridan to Billings, Mont. ran on 24 August 1969 -- eight months before the BN merger and twenty months before Amtrak, neither of which ever ran this corridor. Corrected 2026-08-30 from an earlier drawn end of 1971; frequency estimated/unsourced", "sources": ["Segment-level: end year 1969 sourced to WyoHistory.org, 'The Burlington Route: Wyoming's Second Transcontinental Railroad' -- 'The last scheduled passenger train from Alliance, Neb., through Sheridan to Billings, Mont. ran on Aug. 24, 1969.' Start year 1901 and the headway are NOT sourced at segment level.", "https://www.wyohistory.org/encyclopedia/burlington-route-wyomings-second-transcontinental-railroad"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-102.87837, 42.09443], "to": [-103.06236, 42.31642], "chord_mi": 17.91, "traced_mi": 18.03, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["BNSF Butte Subdivision (18.03 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-98.34987, 40.94639], "to": [-98.61216, 41.0034], "chord_mi": 13.77, "traced_mi": 14.24, "snap_m": [0, 1], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["BNSF Ravenna Subdivision (14.24 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-97.10343, 40.89407], "to": [-97.56235, 40.89394], "chord_mi": 23.09, "traced_mi": 23.98, "snap_m": [0, 0], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["BNSF Ravenna Subdivision (23.98 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.0 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m"}], "geometry_quality": "Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 1 ruled segment totalling 18 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed). Straight-line repair 2026-08-29: 3 ruled segments totalling 55 mi replaced with OpenStreetMap-traced rail geometry (see geometry_repairs for the OSM lines each one followed)."}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-96.71414, 40.8135], [-96.71443, 40.81128], [-96.71828, 40.80673], [-96.7193, 40.80734], [-96.72119, 40.80764], [-96.72613, 40.80752], [-96.73748, 40.80634], [-96.77018, 40.80642], [-96.77579, 40.80769], [-96.79238, 40.80781], [-96.7976, 40.80851], [-96.80329, 40.81062], [-96.81435, 40.81731], [-96.81824, 40.8192], [-96.82492, 40.82077], [-96.83115, 40.82067], [-96.85211, 40.81682], [-96.85753, 40.81502], [-96.8629, 40.81138], [-96.87086, 40.80235], [-96.87714, 40.79895], [-96.88164, 40.79783], [-96.89678, 40.79541], [-96.9591, 40.77349], [-96.9665, 40.77304], [-96.99511, 40.77615], [-97.03086, 40.77374], [-97.04221, 40.77388], [-97.0462, 40.77436], [-97.0505, 40.77593], [-97.05472, 40.77963], [-97.06692, 40.80334], [-97.09493, 40.88819], [-97.09694, 40.89068], [-97.09958, 40.8926], [-97.1034289, 40.8940688], [-97.104473, 40.8942882], [-97.1057304, 40.8944525], [-97.1073802, 40.894557], [-97.1174841, 40.8945996], [-97.1188305, 40.8945935], [-97.126593